**The proportion of 5-EU-positive nuclei did not change consistently with ActD 1 µM.**

We quantified the proportion of 5-EU-positive nuclei in [Cell line] cells ([treatment and duration]) labelled with [antibody or dye for each stain]. Small dots show individual fields, coloured by run; large symbols show the value of each run (the mean of its fields); lines join the same run; horizontal lines show the mean of runs. n = 3 runs per condition; 9 fields per condition; individual fields are not treated as independent replicates. Positive fractions used all evaluable positive and negative nuclei as the denominator. Classification used Otsu thresholding per acquisition date of mean 5-EU intensities; a value strictly above the threshold was positive and equality was negative. Unclassified objects were not selected. Per-run differences (ActD 1 µM − Untreated): +11 pp (Rep1), −29 pp (Rep2) and −58 pp (Rep3). No hypothesis test or confidence interval was calculated because the positivity threshold was not set from a negative control.
